      <flow name="f1">
        <doc>The rate of change of u1: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u1 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(0 - 2 * u1 + u2) / (h * h) + source * u1 * u1</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f2">
        <doc>The rate of change of u2: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u2 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u1 - 2 * u2 + u3) / (h * h) + source * u2 * u2</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f3">
        <doc>The rate of change of u3: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u3 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u2 - 2 * u3 + u4) / (h * h) + source * u3 * u3</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f4">
        <doc>The rate of change of u4: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u4 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u3 - 2 * u4 + u5) / (h * h) + source * u4 * u4</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f5">
        <doc>The rate of change of u5: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u5 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u4 - 2 * u5 + u6) / (h * h) + source * u5 * u5</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f6">
        <doc>The rate of change of u6: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u6 squared.</doc>
