      </flow>
      <flow name="f7">
        <doc>The rate of change of u7: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u7 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u6 - 2 * u7 + u8) / (h * h) + source * u7 * u7</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f8">
        <doc>The rate of change of u8: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u8 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u7 - 2 * u8 + u9) / (h * h) + source * u8 * u8</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f9">
        <doc>The rate of change of u9: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u9 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u8 - 2 * u9 + u10) / (h * h) + source * u9 * u9</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f10">
        <doc>The rate of change of u10: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u10 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u9 - 2 * u10 + u11) / (h * h) + source * u10 * u10</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f11">
        <doc>The rate of change of u11: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u11 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u10 - 2 * u11 + u12) / (h * h) + source * u11 * u11</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f12">
        <doc>The rate of change of u12: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u12 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u11 - 2 * u12 + u13) / (h * h) + source * u12 * u12</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f13">
        <doc>The rate of change of u13: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u13 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u12 - 2 * u13 + u14) / (h * h) + source * u13 * u13</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f14">
        <doc>The rate of change of u14: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u14 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u13 - 2 * u14 + u15) / (h * h) + source * u14 * u14</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f15">
        <doc>The rate of change of u15: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u15 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u14 - 2 * u15 + u16) / (h * h) + source * u15 * u15</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f16">
        <doc>The rate of change of u16: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u16 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u15 - 2 * u16 + u17) / (h * h) + source * u16 * u16</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f17">
        <doc>The rate of change of u17: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u17 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u16 - 2 * u17 + u18) / (h * h) + source * u17 * u17</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f18">
        <doc>The rate of change of u18: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u18 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u17 - 2 * u18 + u19) / (h * h) + source * u18 * u18</eqn>
      </flow>
      <flow name="f19">
        <doc>The rate of change of u19: heat conducted from its neighbours (the ends of the rod are held at 0), plus the heat the rod makes, source times u19 squared.</doc>
        <eqn>(u18 - 2 * u19 + 0) / (h * h) + source * u19 * u19</eqn>
      </flow>
      <aux name="h">
        <doc>The spacing of the points along the rod, which is 1 long.</doc>
        <eqn>0.05</eqn>
      </aux>
      <aux name="source">
        <doc>1: the rod makes heat in proportion to the square of its temperature, and runs away. 0: it only conducts, and cools towards its ends.</doc>
        <eqn>1</eqn>
      </aux>
